diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 97cdb444..298b8c13 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -73,6 +73,8 @@ Initial release of nf-core/scdownstream, created with the [nf-core](https://nf-c
 
 ### `Fixed`
 
+- Skip HUGO-unifier for non-human species and warn when gene symbol unification is requested, by GPT-6.1 Sol ([#389](https://github.com/nf-core/scdownstream/issues/389)) [[#390](https://github.com/nf-core/scdownstream/pull/390)].
+
 - Update scDblFinder to 1.24.10, pin xgboost 3.4.2 and rebuild amd64 and arm64 containers to fix classifier compatibility, by @nictru and GPT-6.1 Sol [[#387](https://github.com/nf-core/scdownstream/pull/387)].
 - Give `QC_REPORT` a task-local temporary directory inside its container without changing the container runtime's host temporary directory, by @nictru and GPT-6.1 Sol [[#385](https://github.com/nf-core/scdownstream/pull/385)].
 - Add PyArrow to the `ADATA_EXTEND` environment so finalisation can load Arrow-backed pandas fragments, and regenerate containers and Conda lock files, by @nictru and GPT-6.1 Sol [[#385](https://github.com/nf-core/scdownstream/pull/385)].
diff --git a/docs/usage.md b/docs/usage.md
index ab6cad84..2acbd304 100644
--- a/docs/usage.md
+++ b/docs/usage.md
@@ -286,6 +286,10 @@ Select the appropriate species with `--species`:
 nextflow run nf-core/scdownstream --input samplesheet.csv --outdir results --species mouse
 ```
 
+HUGO-unifier (`--unify_gene_symbols`) runs only when `--species` is exactly `human`.
+For any other species, the pipeline skips HUGO-unifier and emits a warning if `--unify_gene_symbols` is enabled.
+Species-aware MyGene.info conversion and standard gene and metadata cleanup still run as applicable.
+
 #### Custom gene lists
 
 For other organisms (e.g. rat, zebrafish), you can provide your own gene lists, with one gene symbol per line, via `--s_genes` and `--g2m_genes`:
